{"body":"## Problem\nThe repo is still vulnerable to Windows Explorer noise files like `Thumbs.db`, which can appear as untracked working-tree clutter during normal documentation work. That adds avoidable dirty-state noise and weakens the repo-hygiene contract.\n\n## Desired outcome\nTreat common Windows thumbnail/cache artifacts as explicit ignore/hygiene targets so they do not keep reappearing as untracked distractions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- repo ignore rules exclude `Thumbs.db` (and any closely related Windows thumbnail noise if appropriate)\n- governance/docs guidance stays consistent with the expectation of clean repo state between bounded work turns\n- validation confirms the repo no longer reports `Thumbs.db` as an untracked artifact after cleanup\n\n## Verification\n- ignore-file inspection\n- `git status --short` after cleanup\n","id":"PVTI_lADOA_2mn84BW-uRzgxtN2M","title":"Ignore Windows Thumbs.db repo-noise artifacts","type":"Issue","url":"https://github.com/governance-foundation/vibegov.io/issues/139"}

